WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.256
- Good morning Believe Nation!

00:00:01.256 --> 00:00:04.317
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is Believe,

00:00:04.317 --> 00:00:06.052
and I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:06.052 --> 00:00:09.258
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:09.258 --> 00:00:10.302
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:10.302 --> 00:00:13.422
we're going to today how
to follow your dreams.

00:00:13.422 --> 00:00:15.249
Over to you, Aaron Marino.

00:00:15.249 --> 00:00:17.811
(rooster crows)

00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:20.214
♫ I wake up every morning,

00:00:20.214 --> 00:00:22.866
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:00:22.866 --> 00:00:26.859
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:30.135
- I met a woman that I
helped lose 100 pounds.

00:00:30.135 --> 00:00:31.210
And she came to me and said,

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.334
"Hey, I want to start a fitness center!"

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:35.917
And this, for me, was my dream.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.701
And it was tough, I
didn't make much money,

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.446
it didn't matter because I was happy,

00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:42.940
I was doing something I loved.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.109
We took some loans,
and got some investors.

00:00:46.109 --> 00:00:47.755
There was a big issue with

00:00:47.755 --> 00:00:50.593
one our investors and my business partner,

00:00:50.593 --> 00:00:52.470
and it ultimately ended up

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.011
in lots of legal fights and battles.

00:00:55.011 --> 00:00:58.155
We had to end up shutting
down this business.

00:00:58.155 --> 00:01:00.799
I was dead broke, I was bankrupt.

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:02.175
In order to make ends meet,

00:01:02.175 --> 00:01:05.486
I was driving a beer
cart at a country club.

00:01:05.486 --> 00:01:08.782
And I'm sitting there with
tears rushing down my face,

00:01:08.782 --> 00:01:10.845
because I don't know where to go.

00:01:10.845 --> 00:01:14.808
I was at the lowest point
that I ever have been.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.772
Giving up was never an option.

00:01:16.772 --> 00:01:17.889
The problem was

00:01:17.889 --> 00:01:20.656
that I didn't know what
success looked like anymore.

00:01:20.656 --> 00:01:22.272
But what I do have

00:01:22.272 --> 00:01:26.190
is a dream and a desire to help people.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.431
At the time, there really wasn't anything,

00:01:28.431 --> 00:01:30.964
any resources out there for regular guys

00:01:30.964 --> 00:01:33.369
to get some solid, basic advice on how

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:34.987
to look good and feel great.

00:01:34.987 --> 00:01:37.637
I decided that I was going to help men

00:01:37.637 --> 00:01:40.988
feel better and amazing about themselves.

00:01:40.988 --> 00:01:43.008
So, I have a video camera.

00:01:43.008 --> 00:01:45.843
I was the least tech-savvy
person you'd ever meet.

00:01:45.843 --> 00:01:48.589
But I picked it up and I
decided that I was going to try

00:01:48.589 --> 00:01:51.021
and film a video and put it on YouTube.

00:01:51.021 --> 00:01:52.973
Everything changed for me.

00:01:52.973 --> 00:01:55.962
I found that new vision,
I found that new passion.

00:01:55.962 --> 00:01:59.835
All of a sudden, I had a
voice, I had an audience.

00:01:59.835 --> 00:02:02.647
And I was doing something
that made me feel incredible

00:02:02.647 --> 00:02:05.466
because I realized I was doing something

00:02:05.466 --> 00:02:06.986
to help other people.

00:02:06.986 --> 00:02:09.000
- Most people quit on
their dreams too soon.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.616
They just quit too soon.

00:02:10.616 --> 00:02:12.543
You don't realize that to have success,

00:02:12.543 --> 00:02:14.773
you have to try and try and try and try,

00:02:14.773 --> 00:02:17.159
keep improving and keep
trying to find another way,

00:02:17.159 --> 00:02:18.264
until you eventually hit it,

00:02:18.264 --> 00:02:20.469
and that's the story of
any successful person.

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:22.157
They tried so many different ways

00:02:22.157 --> 00:02:25.025
until they had the thing that
helped them break through.

00:02:25.025 --> 00:02:28.130
And too many quit way too quickly.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:30.828
And you need to explore,
and say yes, and try things

00:02:30.828 --> 00:02:33.711
until you find that thing
that makes you come alive.

00:02:33.711 --> 00:02:35.742
And so for Aaron, it was YouTube.

00:02:35.742 --> 00:02:37.834
He tried all this other
stuff, and nothing was working

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:39.762
and he knew he had
something bigger in them,

00:02:39.762 --> 00:02:43.394
and he didn't want to
play the safe life, right?

00:02:43.394 --> 00:02:45.395
He didn't want to take
that failure and then say,

00:02:45.395 --> 00:02:48.743
"Okay. That's just not going to work."

00:02:48.743 --> 00:02:52.175
"I'm going to go and
work at a retail store."

00:02:52.175 --> 00:02:54.450
Right, he didn't give up
on doing something bigger,

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:57.598
even if he didn't quite even
know what that bigger thing was

00:02:57.598 --> 00:02:58.922
he didn't give up.

00:02:58.922 --> 00:03:00.840
Most people quit right there.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.184
You need to continue to explore.

00:03:03.184 --> 00:03:04.603
He stumbled into YouTube,

00:03:04.603 --> 00:03:08.009
and that became the thing
that he then exploded with.

00:03:08.009 --> 00:03:10.563
For me, it was going to the YMCA.

00:03:10.563 --> 00:03:12.879
And delivering a speech that
was I was super proud of

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:16.576
to go and help entrepreneurs
when they invited me in,

00:03:16.576 --> 00:03:18.450
and only three people showed up.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.441
You know, three people
showed up to a free event.

00:03:21.441 --> 00:03:23.075
How was I ever going to
turn this into a business,

00:03:23.075 --> 00:03:25.529
and make money from it?

00:03:25.529 --> 00:03:27.695
But because I went,
and because I loved it,

00:03:27.695 --> 00:03:30.402
and because I enjoyed it, I had
to find a way to keep going.

00:03:30.402 --> 00:03:32.338
Even if I never made money from it,

00:03:32.338 --> 00:03:35.722
I had to find a way to keep
doing it because I loved it,

00:03:35.722 --> 00:03:37.727
because it became my dream,

00:03:37.727 --> 00:03:40.506
because the feeling that
I got when I was doing it

00:03:40.506 --> 00:03:41.612
was intoxicating.

00:03:41.612 --> 00:03:43.143
I couldn't wait to go and do it again.

00:03:43.143 --> 00:03:46.428
I just found this thing
that helping entrepreneurs

00:03:46.428 --> 00:03:48.855
was something I found so satisfying.

00:03:48.855 --> 00:03:52.196
And so I had to find the way to continue.

00:03:52.196 --> 00:03:53.402
And that's the thing with dreams.

00:03:53.402 --> 00:03:56.180
A lot of times they don't
make sense at the beginning.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.242
You don't quite know how
it's going to work out.

00:03:58.242 --> 00:04:00.954
You don't necessarily have
that final end goal yet,

00:04:00.954 --> 00:04:02.454
because it's brand new,

00:04:02.454 --> 00:04:04.181
because you haven't done anything yet.

00:04:04.181 --> 00:04:05.724
And so you've got to figure it out.

00:04:05.724 --> 00:04:08.207
You won't get to that success
by sitting on the couch

00:04:08.207 --> 00:04:11.086
and thinking and thinking
and thinking and thinking

00:04:11.086 --> 00:04:13.254
and seeing other people
make a lot of money

00:04:13.254 --> 00:04:15.214
and other people going off
and chasing their dreams.

00:04:15.214 --> 00:04:18.020
You have to get up off the
couch and do something.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.181
People often ask me, "When do you quit?"

00:04:20.181 --> 00:04:22.965
And I'm not the guy that
says never, never quit.

00:04:22.965 --> 00:04:24.234
Really the answer comes down to,

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.818
is it still your dream or not?

00:04:25.818 --> 00:04:28.257
Are you still passionate
about this thing or not?

00:04:28.257 --> 00:04:29.965
If it's still your dream,

00:04:29.965 --> 00:04:31.284
and you just haven't figured out a way

00:04:31.284 --> 00:04:32.711
to make it happen yet,

00:04:32.711 --> 00:04:36.434
then you have to keep going,
you have to keep doing it.

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.850
Like Aaron and his transition to YouTube,

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.719
you have to find different
options and keep testing,

00:04:41.719 --> 00:04:43.516
until you find the thing
that's right for you.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.538
The alternative is,

00:04:44.538 --> 00:04:46.616
you're going to live the
rest of your life in regret.

00:04:46.616 --> 00:04:49.770
You're going to think, "I wish
I just gave a little bit more."

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.818
"I wish I tried a little bit harder."

00:04:51.818 --> 00:04:55.949
"I wish I pushed more on
this thing to make it work."

00:04:55.949 --> 00:04:59.702
And you settled for an average life.

00:04:59.702 --> 00:05:03.181
But if you don't have the passion anymore,

00:05:03.181 --> 00:05:05.928
if it just feels like work to you,

00:05:05.928 --> 00:05:07.742
that's when you quit.

00:05:07.742 --> 00:05:10.022
If it's not your dream anymore,

00:05:10.022 --> 00:05:11.610
then you quit and you move on to

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.180
the next thing that is your dream.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.478
So the question of the day today is,

00:05:14.478 --> 00:05:17.818
I'm curious: what is your dream?

00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:19.403
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:05:19.403 --> 00:05:21.015
I'm really curious to find out.

00:05:21.015 --> 00:05:23.828
Write it with some passion,
with emotion, with feelings

00:05:23.828 --> 00:05:25.163
so that when you read it back you're like,

00:05:25.163 --> 00:05:28.681
"Yeah! That's what I'm
doing. I'm pumped about it!"

00:05:28.681 --> 00:05:29.545
Let me see what you got.

00:05:29.545 --> 00:05:30.615
Leave it in the comments.

00:05:30.615 --> 00:05:31.858
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:05:31.858 --> 00:05:34.104
to Eric Seuret from 3smobile,

00:05:34.104 --> 00:05:36.519
Eric, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:05:36.519 --> 00:05:39.276
Your One Word, I really, really,
really appreciate it man,

00:05:39.276 --> 00:05:40.914
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:05:40.914 --> 00:05:43.573
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you.

00:05:43.573 --> 00:05:45.565
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:05:45.565 --> 00:05:47.940
and whatever Your One Word is.

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:48.859
Much love,

00:05:48.859 --> 00:05:51.906
and I'll see you again tomorrow
morning for another shot

00:05:51.906 --> 00:05:52.764
of Entspresso.

00:05:52.764 --> 00:05:55.298
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:05:55.298 --> 00:05:58.965
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:06:01.751 --> 00:06:04.063
- I, I truly believe, and
people throw the word around,

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.464
dreams, it's all about dreams.

00:06:06.464 --> 00:06:08.597
And by the way, dreams cost nothing.

00:06:08.597 --> 00:06:09.793
They're free.

00:06:09.793 --> 00:06:12.071
Uh, the hard part is
just keeping them going,

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:13.734
and please, keep them going.

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:16.444
Because we're here for one simple reason.

00:06:16.444 --> 00:06:19.191
He believed in the dream,
I believed in the dream,

00:06:19.191 --> 00:06:20.488
and our dreams come true,

00:06:20.488 --> 00:06:23.707
and there's no reason every
one of yours can't either.

00:06:23.707 --> 00:06:25.457
Thank you very much.

00:06:26.538 --> 00:06:29.472
- It sounds so cheesy,
but follow your dreams.

00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:33.372
Like for me, I have 100
percent belief in that if

00:06:33.372 --> 00:06:36.519
somebody really wants
something and really has the,

00:06:36.519 --> 00:06:38.507
and really is eager to work hard for it,

00:06:38.507 --> 00:06:39.819
you can make it happen

00:06:39.819 --> 00:06:42.206
or you can at least be
very very close, you know.

00:06:42.206 --> 00:06:43.039
So, yeah.

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.989
It sounds cheesy but follow your dreams,

00:06:46.989 --> 00:06:49.467
and spend as much time as
you can trying to improve,

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.206
get better, learn new things,

00:06:51.206 --> 00:06:53.773
and it's never too late
to learn new things.

00:06:53.773 --> 00:06:55.880
For me still, every day
I get to learn new things

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.521
and that's the fun thing.

00:06:57.521 --> 00:06:58.905
You never know everything.

00:06:58.905 --> 00:07:02.895
Every single morning, Monday
through Fridays at 9:00 AM,

00:07:02.895 --> 00:07:07.195
I host a live call-in radio
show on Sirius satellite radio.

00:07:07.195 --> 00:07:09.608
It's called Make it
Happen with Mel Robbins.

00:07:09.608 --> 00:07:13.621
And the thing that's been
so crazy about that show is,

00:07:13.621 --> 00:07:17.741
every single person that
calls me on that show,

00:07:17.741 --> 00:07:21.887
they call in because they're
feeling stuck in their lives,

00:07:21.887 --> 00:07:23.875
and they're resigned about their ability

00:07:23.875 --> 00:07:25.028
to change their lives.

00:07:25.028 --> 00:07:27.257
And I'm not talking about
people that are nuts.

00:07:27.257 --> 00:07:30.268
I'm talking about successful
people like you and me,

00:07:30.268 --> 00:07:32.568
that just somehow got
stuck in their lives.

00:07:32.568 --> 00:07:33.593
And I'm not talking about people

00:07:33.593 --> 00:07:35.685
that are looking for cheesy self-help,

00:07:35.685 --> 00:07:37.276
I'm talking about people that really want

00:07:37.276 --> 00:07:39.991
to figure out how to
move themselves forward.

00:07:39.991 --> 00:07:42.759
And I find that so many of
us think that our dreams

00:07:42.759 --> 00:07:45.165
are unreachable, or unrealistic,

00:07:45.165 --> 00:07:47.082
and it's just so sad.

00:07:47.082 --> 00:07:50.732
I mean, people think that
their dreams disappear.

00:07:50.732 --> 00:07:53.718
And if that's what you
think, congratulations,

00:07:53.718 --> 00:07:55.351
you're officially stuck.

00:07:55.351 --> 00:07:58.729
And the truth is that our
dreams are always there,

00:07:58.729 --> 00:08:01.071
and they don't ever give up on us,

00:08:01.071 --> 00:08:02.608
we give up on them.

00:08:02.608 --> 00:08:06.549
But here's the secret. If
you just force yourself,

00:08:06.549 --> 00:08:08.549
and I mean force, because I know damn well

00:08:08.549 --> 00:08:10.801
none of you want to do
anything about this.

00:08:10.801 --> 00:08:12.329
And I also know you're sitting there like,

00:08:12.329 --> 00:08:14.681
"Yeah, this self help
crap, this isn't for me."

00:08:14.681 --> 00:08:19.043
But if you just force yourself
to take a couple small steps

00:08:19.043 --> 00:08:21.210
there's always a surprise.

